[require map::box::entry [opt [vset VERSION]]]
[description]

This package provides a [package map::display] attachment extending the map's behaviour.
This attachment enables the user to enter a (bounding) [term geo/box].

[para] While editing is enabled the user creates the box with the mouse:

[list_begin itemized]
[item] Clicking mouse button 1 on the map places a corner. After two corners the box is complete:
the editor adds the missing corners and draws the box. No further corners can be placed while the
box exists.
[item] Dragging a corner with mouse button 2 moves it, resizing the box.
[item] Clicking mouse button 1 on a corner removes the whole box, making way for a new one.
[list_end]

[para] Panning and zooming the map work as usual. On zoom changes the box is redrawn at its
geographical location.

[para] The attachment knows the zoom level and the viewport of the map only from the view changes
the map reports through its option [option -on-view-change]. Therefore create the attachment
before the map reports its view for the first time, i.e. right after creating the map, or move or
zoom the map (e.g. with its method [method center]) afterwards. Until the attachment knows the zoom
level of the map, no box can be entered or set.

[section API]

[list_begin definitions]
[call [cmd ::map::box::entry] [arg objectName] [arg map] [opt [arg options]...]]

Creates a new box entry attachment [arg objectName] for the [package map::display] widget
[arg map], configured with the specified options. The result of the command is the fully
qualified name of the new object. The command is also available as [cmd {map box entry}].

[para] The attachment takes over the option [option -on-view-change] of [arg map]. The previous
value of that option is remembered and still invoked for each view change. Do not change that
option of the map after creating the attachment.

[para] Editing is initially disabled. Use method [method enable] to enable it.

[para] The attachment supports the following option:

[list_begin options]
[opt_def -on-box-change [arg cmdprefix]]

A command prefix which is invoked when the box was changed, with one additional argument, the new
box. The box is a list of four numbers, the minimal latitude, minimal longitude, maximal latitude,
and maximal longitude, in this order, as in the [const geo] element of a [term geo/box] value
described in [package map::box::file]. It is the empty list when the box was removed. The result
of the command is ignored.

[para] The command is invoked for changes made by the user, and by method [method clear], but not
by method [method set].

[para] The default is the empty string, i.e. changes are not reported.

[list_end]
[list_end]

The attachment supports the standard methods [method cget] and [method configure], and the
following methods:

[list_begin definitions]
[call [arg objectName] [method enable]]

Enables editing of the box by the user. The result of the method is the empty string.

[call [arg objectName] [method disable]]

Disables editing of the box by the user. The box stays visible. The result of the method is the
empty string.

[call [arg objectName] [method active]]

Returns a boolean value, [const true] if editing is enabled, and [const false] otherwise.

[call [arg objectName] [method box]]

Returns the current box, in the format described for option [option -on-box-change], or the empty
list if there is no box.

[call [arg objectName] [method set] [arg geobox]]

Shows the box [arg geobox], in the format described for option [option -on-box-change], replacing
the current box, and then centers and zooms the map to fit the box, as method [method fit] does.

[para] The result of the method is the empty string.

[call [arg objectName] [method clear]]

Removes the current box. The result of the method is the empty string.

[call [arg objectName] [method fit]]

Centers the map on the current box, at the highest zoom level at which the whole box is visible.
Does nothing if there is no box.

[para] The result of the method is the empty string.

[list_end]

[section EXAMPLE]

[example {
package require map::provider::osm
package require map::display
package require map::box::entry

map provider osm tiles [file join $env(HOME) .cache osm-tiles]
map display .map -provider tiles -initial-geo {48.05 11.1} -initial-zoom 10
pack .map -fill both -expand 1

map box entry boxentry .map -on-box-change {apply {{geobox} {
    puts "box: $geobox"
}}}
boxentry enable
}]

